---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FurtherReading from '../components/FurtherReading.astro';
import SeaBreak from '../components/SeaBreak.astro';
import { celestial, scenes } from '../config/images';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CTABand from '../components/CTABand.astro';
const crumbs = [{ label: 'How Readings Work', href: '/how-readings-work/' }];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How Readings Work. What to expect"
  description="What happens in an astrology reading with Mo Lumen: booking, intake, preparation, the conversation itself, and what you take home."
  path="/how-readings-work/"
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
  <section class="hero hero--split">
    <div class="container">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What to expect</p>
        <h1>How readings work</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          You do not need to know astrology or arrive with the perfect question. I prepare the
          chart, guide the conversation, explain what I am seeing, and leave room for your own
          experience to make the interpretation more specific.
        </p>
      </div>
      <img
        class="hero__img"
        src={scenes.readingProcess.src}
        srcset={scenes.readingProcess.srcset}
        sizes="100vw"
        alt={scenes.readingProcess.alt}
        width={scenes.readingProcess.width}
        height={scenes.readingProcess.height}
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">The short version</p>
      <h2>Before, during, after</h2>
      <div class="grid grid--3" style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Before</h3>
          <p>You book, send the birth information the reading needs, and tell me what is bringing you in. I prepare the chart before we meet.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>During</h3>
          <p>I explain the patterns and timing I am seeing. You can ask questions, add context, disagree, or simply listen while the picture develops.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>After</h3>
          <p>You receive the recording and the chart materials included with your reading, so you do not need to take notes while we talk.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <div class="callout" style="margin-top: var(--space-7);">
        <p style="margin: 0;"><strong>Your part is simpler than you may think.</strong> Bring accurate birth information if you have it and whatever is genuinely on your mind. Knowing the astrology is my responsibility, not yours.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container prose flow">
      <p class="eyebrow">What collaboration means</p>
      <h2>The chart gives me possibilities. Your life helps me understand which ones matter.</h2>
      <p>
        Suppose I notice a pattern that can describe several different ways of handling effort,
        pressure, or responsibility. I will not choose one version simply because it sounds neat on
        paper. I may explain what I am seeing and ask where, if anywhere, you recognize it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your answer gives me information the chart cannot provide by itself. Maybe the pattern is
        obvious in your work but not in your relationships. Maybe it was stronger earlier in life.
        Maybe another part of the chart changes how it is expressed. That is not the reading going
        off script. That is the reading becoming more accurate to the person sitting with me.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is why I think of a reading as synthesis rather than a performance. Technique gets us
        somewhere important; conversation helps us understand how the technique is actually being
        lived.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SeaBreak image={celestial.lighthouse} />

  <section class="section section--sea">
    <div class="container prose flow">
      <h2>Before we meet</h2>
      <p>
        When you book, you'll choose a time shown in your own time zone, pay securely online, and
        complete a short intake form with the information needed for that reading. You can tell me
        what is bringing you in and include questions you already know you want to explore. Then
        you'll receive preparation notes by email. There is nothing to study.
      </p>

      <h2>If your birth time is uncertain</h2>
      <p>
        Birth time affects the ascendant, angles, and house structure, so I want to know both the
        time and how certain it is. An uncertain time does not make the rest of the chart disappear.
        If you do not know yours, the <a href="/birth-time/">Birth Time guide</a> explains what can
        still be used and what is better left open. We can shape the reading around what is solid.
      </p>

      <h2>During the session</h2>
      <p>
        We meet one-on-one over Zoom or phone; in-person meetings in DFW can sometimes be arranged.
        I will have studied your chart beforehand. I explain what I see and why I am looking there,
        and I may ask how a possible pattern is showing up in your life.
      </p>
      <p>
        You are welcome to ask questions and interrupt. You are equally welcome to listen for a
        while before you know what you want to say. Some readings become conversational quickly;
        others unfold more quietly. I will guide either one.
      </p>

      <h2>What you take home</h2>
      <p>
        Every live session includes a recording and a copy of your chart. A second listen can be
        useful because you can hear the conversation again without also having to absorb it for the
        first time.
      </p>

      <h2>What a reading will not do for you</h2>
      <p>
        Most readings are about perspective, pattern recognition, and timing rather than telling
        you which decision to make. Some branches of astrology, including horary, are designed to
        address a specific question more directly; when I use them, I will be clear about what the
        technique supports and what it does not. Astrology is not medical, psychological, legal, or
        financial advice. See the <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a> for the full boundaries.
      </p>
      <p>Your birth details and session information are treated as sensitive. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for how that information is handled.</p>
      <FurtherReading />
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABand
    heading="Bring what is actually on your mind."
    body="You do not need to prepare the perfect question or know the astrology. I will bring the chart and the preparation; we will take it from there together."
    buttonLabel="Find the Reading That Fits"
    buttonHref="/reading-finder/"
    secondaryLabel="See all readings"
    secondaryHref="/readings/"
  />
</BaseLayout>
